  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nShower activity, mainly across far northeast Ohio and northwest\nPA early this morning, with embedded thunderstorms will move\neast of the area during the early morning hours, with primarily\ndry conditions expected across the forecast area through the\nremainder of the morning. Additional showers and a few storms \nmay develop ahead of a slow moving cold front this afternoon, \nprimarily across the far southern and eastern portions of the \nforecast area, but this activity would be fairly isolated if it \nmanifests. Severe risk is low given lack of deep layer flow, but\nsufficient destabilization may result in a non-zero chance of \nstronger brief updrafts that could result in a few strong wind \ngusts. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nAs ridging builds across the region this weekend into next week,\ntemperatures will be on the rise with highs in the upper 80s to\nlow 90s by Monday and Tuesday. Heat indices in the mid 90s will\nbe possible during this time before the ridge flattens a bit\nover the Great Lakes by mid/late week.",
